/* US ZIP code centroids, 42,555 of them, packed.

   Layout. Records are sorted by ZIP and grouped by the first three digits.
   DIR holds 1,001 three-character offsets, one per prefix plus a terminator,
   so a lookup jumps straight to its group and scans at most 99 records. BODY
   holds eight characters per record: the last two ZIP digits, then latitude
   and longitude as three base-64 characters each.

   Latitude is stored at 1/1000 of a degree and longitude at 1/500, which puts
   the worst round-trip error at about 390 feet. A ZIP centroid is already a
   crude stand-in for a home address several miles wide, and the model clamps
   distance at the 85th percentile of past guest lists, so that error is far
   below anything the forecast can resolve.

   335 KB here, about 214 KB over the wire once the server gzips it. Nothing is
   parsed at load: lookups read the string directly, so there is no startup
   cost and no 42,555-entry object sitting in memory.

   Regenerate from the npm 'zipcodes' package. */

